    "descriptionEn": "Sophy Pagoda, also known as Koh Koh, has left traces of genocidal crimes, including handcuffs, and is housed in a shrine with some remains unearthed around the pagoda in the 1980s. The house of remains is at the south-east of the Buddhist temple. Every year, on the 20th of May, there are 100 monks prays and hundreds of people come to the site to pray and make dedication to the dead. While digging the land in about 0.5 meter deep to build the new monk’s hut (Kodi), they saw clothing, and bones buried. Those later were taken to be place with other remains exist. The night the remains found, there was monk dreamt of a crowd of people walked toward the Buddhist temple.",
