    "descriptionEn": "Huang Waterfall is a natural tourism site with beautiful views and fresh air in Tbong Kmum province, but not many non-locals recognize it, except the locals, since it is located a little far from the national road, and lack of road signs. Tourists will be more relaxed when arriving Asrom Huang Waterfall Resort or Wat Kuhea Sela Moha Barmei Kongkea Huang, where they see eye-catching natural view of cascading waterfall. Asrom Huang Waterfall locates in the area of Wat Kuhea Sela Moha Barmei Kongkea Huang. The water flows from the high stream which is in O Chheu Teal village, Teuk Chrov commune, about 3 km away from the upper part to the Srae Veng village. The waterfall appeals its combination beauty of high cliff cascading waterfall, rock cave, shady trees, vines, and swingy roots of plants along the both side of the edges. The resort has welcomed mostly local tourists since 1997. Huang waterfall, a cliff-hiking area with dozens of square meters of cascading waterfalls with beautiful views and fresh air, covers an area of 1800 hectares.",
