    "descriptionEn": "At the top of a mountain about 50 meters high, called Phnom Kambor, is a temple with three towers, which is very dilapidated. Today, only one wall remains and there is a pond at the foot of the mountain, and today it is built as a village hall. In the narrow perimeter of the top of the mountain, one can see the foundations of three towers built parallel to each other, facing three, of which today only the north tower remains a wall. Remains of sandstone temple building materials include white pieces, diamonds, unfinished carvings, stair steps, etc. These pink sandstones come from neighboring Phnom Preah Net Preah.",
