    "descriptionEn": "The brick temple has a sandstone doorway. The temple has four gates, the real gate in the east three is a false gate in the other direction. Carved out of sandstone, the triangular walls and roofs have been ripped off. There are stones left to store cross-shaped relics. Today, many underground temples have lost their original appearance, but a new gate has been erected in front of them. There are other ancient medieval stupas in the pagoda complex, which is probably why the pagoda is called Lotte Pagoda. According to the CISARK listing, across the stream next to the pagoda fence, there is another ancient ruined temple called Prasat Lo, but only a few remains remain.",
