    "descriptionEn": "Prasat Phas is a ruined temple, only two walls remain, which looks very miserable. The temple is located within the compound of Pheas Pagoda, to the south there is a large pool. The temple has three towers, with two towers on each side. On the walls are carved statues of small deities, a kind of floating temple attached to the wall. According to locals, during the war, armed groups came to remove the artifacts from the temple, but could not be removed due to the power of the sacred objects. . Today, the artifacts are kept in museums. The temple is surrounded by a moat and surmounted by a bridge built by the Buddhists at the foot of the pagoda. In terms of structure, this temple should be a hospital or guesthouse along Angkor Thom Road towards Sdok Kak Thom, built during the reign of Jayavarman VII.",
