    "descriptionEn": "The Calf Rohal Kes Avean, at the confluence of the Serei Sophorn and Mongkul Borei rivers, has become a conservation area with tens of thousands of fish and birds and an attractive ecotourism destination. History and Geography \"Veal Hal Kes Avien\" is a diversion dam of the irrigation system built in the era of Democratic Kampuchea. This area has an area of ​​water and flooded forest of about 28 hectares, which can be divided into two: the first is the dry land area, a conservation area for mixed fish with the size of 5 hectares called dry land . The second part is a flooded forest area where a diverse group of birds lay eggs and feed on tens of thousands of 23 hectares area. It has the shape of an intestine, called intestine. The common name of this sanctuary is called Rohal Kes Avien, which has tens of thousands of birds, about 10 species. The Ministry of Environment will cooperate with the Provincial Department of Tourism to propose the establishment of the Veal Rohal Kes Avean Ecotourism Area.",
