    "descriptionEn": "Crowds, mostly young people from Thmar Puok and Svay Chek districts, visit Ta Meng Dam, which is a diversion dam, during the rainy season. This seasonal seaside resort is located behind the dam of some villages in the municipality of Kork Kathin. Ang Ta Meng was a regime in Democratic Kampuchea which was restored by local authorities, and eventually the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology was rebuilt and expanded to 5,300 cubic meters. This basin receives water from the plateau of the Preah hills and the Dangrek mountain range and can irrigate thousands of hectares of rice fields in Thmar Puok and Svay Chek districts, and the rest will go to the Ang Trapeang basin. Thmor. In the pool there are many species of natural Khmer fish.",
