    "descriptionEn": "A large basin that contains water for irrigation, agriculture and daily use by locals has become a potential tourist destination for locals and tourists, transforming it from an illegal fishing area in the past . The pedestal pool is over 2,000 meters long and over 1,000 meters wide and has a large body of water that looks out with the naked eye. Originally the location was a quiet forest but later turned into a tourist destination with lots of locals where you can watch the sunset, take a boat ride, watch the birds and have a spot to eat. Ang Cheung Kruos has a pontoon bridge and harbor where tourists can sit and take souvenir photos, and there are plans to build a pontoon bridge to cross to Koh Samrong in the middle of the pool and also an ancient cemetery.",
