    "descriptionEn": "Ang Trapeang Thmor is connected to National Road 6 by the largest reservoir in the country after Tonle Sap, which is a natural reservoir. The water is clear and cool, so many tourists like to visit and become a big resort. People built stalls made of the same bamboo, thatched, clean and suitable for tourists to relax and eat easily. In the water there are fun entertainment services such as airbags, boats, boats and adequate rescue preparations. The food is reasonably priced and hygienic. Ang Trapeang Thmor is a conservation area for many rare species of birds, such as Gray Crane, Tapa, and Colored Forest. It should be noted that birds as well as squid, reptile fish in Ang Trapeang Thmor Conservation Area may or may not be present depending on their species and the season. Some animals migrate for seasonal food, while others find food and roost constantly, especially in the presence of red-headed cranes.",
