    "descriptionEn": "The museum was built in 2004 with the support of the Royal Government of Cambodia. The museum is located in the city and is built in the Khmer style. Funding for the museum comes from the cost of borrowing artifacts for exhibitions abroad. There are many artifacts such as stone statues, wooden statues, temple ornaments, pottery, bronze objects and metal in the museum. All these collections are collected from distant temples and ancient sites in the province. Some items were obtained from locals found while farming and others were confiscated from antique dealers along the Thai border. The museum is a place that helps promote the reputation of the Cambodian people and the culture of presenting the past. It is also a place to show the relationship with the place where we live, the relationship with objects and events of the past.",
