    "descriptionEn": "The bones transported from the slaughterhouse in Prey Kork, Trach, Kork, Tamol and other places in Phnom Srok district were laid in a monument at Monisathavat Pagoda, also known as Bo Pagoda. Many skulls and limbs deposited in this monument have been broken and rotted. Later, another stupa was built in the compound of Sovannkha Sattharam Pagoda, called Kandal Pagoda, to place the remains, which were then transported for storage.",
