    "descriptionEn": "The waterfall is more than 20 meters high, accompanied by small and large trees, the water is very cold and little known. Tourists must travel patiently to visit the magnificent Kbal Damrey Waterfall. This place has a very nice view, especially in the rainy season, when there is a lot of water, it is beautiful, while in the dry season, there is only a small amount of water. The forest road trip lasts more than 3 hours, walking in reverse along the flowing water from Sang Santivan forest area or called \"O'Me area\". Note that the forest route requires a guide as it can be dangerous to walk over landmines or wildlife traps. Tourists should also be prepared to pack food and contact a guide.",
