    "descriptionEn": "Kiri Chet Pagoda, also known as Phnom Koy Pagoda, is one of the oldest pagodas in Pailin province. This pagoda was famous for housing dozens of crocodiles, and some of them are still standing today. This pagoda was built in 1880 and the name of the pagoda is due to the presence of a location next to a mountain, the top of which has the shape of a stupa, while the locals call Pagoda Phnom Koy from the name from the village of Phnom Koy. . In the past, near this pagoda, there was a leafy forest and many crocodiles, but these crocodiles had the power not to do anything to people and now there are not many of them. Nearby there is a river with a beautiful view can also take a boat trip.",
