    "descriptionEn": "Currently, Phnom Kach Phka is organized by the pagoda committee and has more than 300 steps to climb to the top of the mountain. The name Phnom Kach Phka has a story that there was once a general who was the right arm of Khleang Moeung who traveled to Thailand and passed through a temporary residence in this area. Living near the foot of the mountain, she loves fruit and water on the ridge. On the hillside, there is a sacred well surrounded by colorful flowers, and every day she goes to cut flowers to offer to the gods near the sacred well. The captain who secretly fell in love with the woman named the mountain Phnom Kach Phka. Here is a beautiful natural beauty and on the ridge there is also a holy well where people often go to pray and ask for water to drink or dive for healing. This hill station has large boulders stacked on top of each other, a rare sight, and one can also look down from the top of the mountain to see the vast rice fields. In this mountain, there is a cave that must go down to the top of the mountain. The pagoda here is a shrine where people often go to worship there in large numbers.",
