    "descriptionEn": "The OChoam Waterfall was discovered in 2003 by the people who went to live there. In 2007, people who go there often encounter a strange thing, the waterfall cannot be seen. According to the belief of the people there, he said the waterfall was guarded. Until late 2013, environmental officials and the community of O'Choam Nature Reserve cooperated to prepare for the entrance of this station. The waterfall is 30 meters high, surrounded by large rocks and a pond, which is the source of water flowing to this waterfall. The access road to the station has many features such as forests, valleys, streams, rocks and waterfalls in stages from the base of the mountain to the top of the mountain, which makes it fun for children to visit. tourists. The waterfall has two stages up to 3 km apart, the upper stage at a high waterfall and the lower stage is at the foot of the mountain accessible by car.",
