    "descriptionEn": "Sek Sak is a steep river flowing over rocky terrain and has a steep slope of about 500 meters, accompanied by small and large plants and a cool shaded bamboo forest. Sek Sak Resort has emerged over an area of ​​several hectares, which in addition to natural design, there are many other unique landscapes for entertainment. Throughout the park, there are many types of trees that provide shade for guests to relax. There is a pond with clear water and a duck and geese pedal for guests. There are many statues between the trees, but among them the most interesting is the couple of male and female parrots, symbol of the festival, accompanied by a song by Sin Sisamouth describing the site. At the mouth of Stung Sangke, a group of young people take a bath and play happily.",
