    "descriptionEn": "The \"Kanghot\" irrigation dam is the largest of all irrigation dams in Cambodia. The huge \"Kanghot\" dam was built by a Chinese company at a cost of around $60 million initially and could go on to cost tens of millions more to provide adequate and efficient water. The people who use this water are the districts of Banan, Sangke, Ek Phnom and Thmor Koul. The \"Kanghot\" dam dates back to the times of Democratic Kampuchea (Khmer Rouge regime), when thousands of people were used to build the dam for irrigation purposes, as well as Sangke dams at the same time.",
