    "descriptionEn": "The Sopheak Monkul water park has a swimming pool for adults, a swimming pool for children, a beautiful flower garden for the background, a restaurant and a slide for the little ones up to Angkor Wat, made of old tires, and most importantly a sea wave pool. The waves rippled on the slopes of the red, yellow and white tiles for children to play with the waves created by the machine at a depth of 1.80 meters. For parents and guardians who don't have time to take their children to see the sea, this water park in Battambang offers a variety of recreational activities. In addition to the four swimming pools, flower gardens, restaurants and fish ponds, this theme park recycles old materials to make the garden more attractive and environmentally friendly. In the future, the center plans to build a long canal for guests to take a boat so that guests can come to the same place to play all kinds of things.",
